NRR 1.0

Code is speech. The Grantor projects this Work into the commons of the
internet, for everyone to transform, monetize, distribute, or otherwise use
without permission or attribution. The intent is freedom under every
jurisdiction, across all spans of time and space, for eternity.

1. Scope

The "Work" is material expressly offered under NRR 1.0. A "Grantor" is a
person or entity offering rights it owns or is authorized to grant in that
material. Each Grantor acts only for those rights. Separately licensed
material and rights controlled by others are outside this grant.

2. Dedication to the commons

To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, each Grantor irrevocably
dedicates the Work to the public domain and abandons and waives all copyright
and related rights it controls in the Work, including database rights and
rights of attribution and integrity. This dedication covers every territory,
every medium and technology now known or later developed, and the entire
duration of those rights, including extensions, renewals and revivals.

3. Unconditional fallback permission

Where any dedication or waiver is ineffective, each Grantor automatically
grants every person and entity an irrevocable, perpetual, worldwide,
nonexclusive, royalty-free, fully paid-up, transferable and sublicensable
license to exercise those rights for any purpose, commercial or otherwise.
This includes using, studying, running, copying, modifying, translating,
transforming, combining, making derivative works, publishing, communicating,
displaying, performing, distributing, selling, monetizing and relicensing
the Work, in whole or in part, in source, executable or any other form.

No permission request, payment, attribution, copyright notice, copy of this
license, disclosure of source, disclosure of changes, or use of any particular
license is required. You may keep changes private or distribute them under
terms of your choice. No later action by a Grantor withdraws freedoms already
granted under NRR for material already offered under it.

4. Patents and other controlled rights

Each Grantor also grants an irrevocable, perpetual, worldwide, nonexclusive,
royalty-free, fully paid-up, transferable and sublicensable patent license
to make, have made, use, offer for sale, sell, import and otherwise exploit
the Work, under any patent claims it owns or controls that those authorized
acts would otherwise infringe. This does not license claims controlled by
others or claims that are not implicated by the Work.

To the fullest extent permitted by law, each Grantor waives, licenses or
covenants not to assert any other rights it controls in the Work that would
restrict these freedoms.

5. Limits of a grant

NRR grants rights; it cannot override mandatory law, grant another person's
rights, or make unlawful conduct lawful. No author's endorsement is implied.
The references to all time, space and jurisdictions express the broadest
possible grant wherever and for as long as the law allows it to operate.

6. No warranty or liability

THE WORK IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND,
EXPRESS, IMPLIED OR STATUTORY, INCLUDING TITLE, MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR
A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED
BY LAW, NO GRANTOR IS LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGE OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING
FROM OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE WORK OR ITS USE, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT
OR OTHERWISE. LIABILITY THAT CANNOT LAWFULLY BE EXCLUDED IS NOT EXCLUDED.

7. Maximum continuing effect

If any provision is ineffective, it applies to the maximum lawful extent
and the remaining provisions continue. Failure of a waiver does not defeat
the fallback license. No provision is intended to impose a condition on
exercising the granted rights.

This license text itself is offered under NRR 1.0 and may be copied, changed
and used without attribution or permission.
